# Abilities a copy effect gives an object are linked only to one another (CR 607.5, 707.2): Emperor of Bones A exiles Bot2's
# Ornithopter at the beginning of combat with its printed ability. Two turns later Mirrorweave makes A a copy of Emperor of
# Bones B until end of turn - the same text, acquired by the copy effect - and Bot1 adapts A: the +1/+1 counters trigger
# its copied "put a creature card exiled with this creature onto the battlefield", which refers only to what the copied
# exile ability exiled. The Ornithopter stays in exile.

